o  says city officials agreed to the  purchase of nearly 300 000 packages of  ivermectin worth an estimated 1.5  million dollars  they looked at the fact that large  quantities of the drug were bought  especially when the news of its possible  use first emerged  but that's a very bad justification from  the mexico city secretary of health  who said it was what they had based on  available evidence  but there was no evidence  mexico city has stopped distributing  ivermectin but the drug is still being  promoted by vaccine skeptics  misinformation that can cost lives  [Music]  during the pandemic many people around  the world took comfort in long-standing  traditions  celebrating festivals and reviving old  customs helps sustain families and  communities  so too in the mainly indigenous regions  of ecuador  every year in june the indigenous  communities of northern ecuador  celebrate intirami the sun festival  although in many parts of the country  this ancient ritual didn't take place  during the pandemic  blanca bonilla is a traditional healer  she works as a volunteer advisor to  local authorities in the kotakachi  region  when we heard there were covert cases in  the coastal area and also in other  countries  we had a clear plan about what we would  do once it reached our region  we made lots of positive progress with  our experiments fighting the virus  authorities and quechua villages work  hard to maintain a relationship of trust  the indigenous community's hierarchical  structures are respected and valued  and that didn't change during the  pandemic  we never thought it would hit us this  hard  our country and our communities  after the government ordered a lockdown  we had to take matters into our own  hands  but it wasn't all that hard  everyone here has their own garden  everyone stores produce  kotakachi canton has a population of  roughly 40 000 spread across urban and  rural parishes  the main industries are tourism and  agriculture  there were fewer covet infections here  than in other parts of ecuador  [Music]  in 2020 and 2021 the health office here  in kotakachi canton registered  1755 cases  30 patients died and 1715  patients recovered  [Music]  despite the restrictions in the last two  years  some remote rural communities chose to  celebrate the intirami festival of the  sun as usual  [Music]  when the pandemic went global it also  had an impact here in the countryside  it didn't only affect people's health  it affected celebrations and cultural  life here in the canton  is famous for its cultural life and  music there are many artists here it was  a blow for culture  for some communities in the andes and  ecuador the last two years had some  benefits they revived many of the  customs of their ancestors  many of our communities welcomed the  fact that young people began using  medicinal herbs again  for people who live in the countryside  all plants have medicinal value  our knowledge was handed down to us by  our mothers and grandmothers  by our elders by our neighbors  we're gradually acquiring more expertise  and sharing it with other communities  save our lives it was incredible  on june 24th and 25th the quechua  communities will celebrate in tirami and  the village squares will be filled with  life  that's all for this edition of our covet  19 special with a focus on the  environmental impact of the pandemic  next week we'll take stock of where  things stand in the pandemic right now  and check out some of the new research  on covid19 for now thanks for watching  and see you soon  [Music]  you
 

